  "manualWindowsVerification": {
    "$comment": "These checks CANNOT run on Linux. A human operator must perform them on real Windows 11 hardware against the COMPILED WindowsReferenceWpf app, recording evidence per docs/testing/windows-m3-manual-checklist.md.",
    "steps": [
      "Build WindowsReferenceWpf.csproj on Windows 11 with the .NET 10 Desktop SDK and confirm it launches without elevation.",
      "Confirm a real UIA capture of the running app produces the AutomationIds and control types in uiaSource above (MainWindow, UsernameEdit, PasswordEdit, RoleCombo, SubmitButton, ResultsList, DeleteAllButton, CrashButton, ResetButton).",
      "Confirm the PasswordEdit value is captured masked, never in cleartext, in the Trace and Artifacts.",
      "Confirm clicking DeleteAllButton triggers a per-action local approval prompt in the Companion and that a denial leaves the list unchanged.",
      "Confirm clicking CrashButton yields a deterministic crash Finding that the Oracle does not suppress.",
      "Confirm the Reset entry and the reset helper restore the initial local-JSON state.",
      "Confirm Job Object cleanup: after shutdown, verify via Task Manager / Process Explorer that no WindowsReferenceWpf.exe process survives and that an unrelated same-name process started outside the Job is untouched."
    ]
